DiagHam CMake migration
Contribution copyright (C) 2026 Paul Watford <paulwatford@netherpixelstudios.net>

This repository contains the DiagHam source code (copyright its authors, see
AUTHORS) together with a CMake build system, a test suite and a small number
of fixes to the DiagHam sources. The DiagHam history is preserved on the
`upstream` branch; every change made here is an ordinary commit on `main`.

What this contribution adds:
  - a CMake build system (CMakeLists.txt, CMakePresets.json, cmake/, the
    generated per-directory CMakeLists.txt files and
    scripts_cmake/extract_autotools.py that produces them);
  - a ctest suite (tests/) and benchmark material (benchmarks/);
  - fixes to upstream DiagHam files, each an individual commit whose message
    records the change and its rationale; patches/PATCHES.md is the audit
    trail (as required by GNU GPL section 2a).

